      "change_claim": "Title: Distill dimension-tagged review patterns and make retrieval paper- and rubric-sensitive\n- Diagnosis: memory returned the identical four cross-domain episodes for every paper (QUAL 0.50/0.49/0.47/0.43 for both Trust-Region MARL and GNN-gradient-flow) with one metadata tag `{role, topic}`; metrics show saturated grounding (4.8-5.0) but weak Correct./Thoro. (2.75-3.1 / 1.8-2.44), i.e., style transfer instead of dimension coverage, plus foreign-anchor reuse.\n- Memory design: KnowledgeItem gains kind/pattern/polarity/subcategory/evidence_requirement/revision_template/source_id/keywords; write stores a distilled PATTERN CARD plus the verbatim EPISODE with role/kind/topic/subcategory/polarity/source/keyword metadata and a Jaccard near-duplicate guard; deterministic opinion-block parsing backfills card fields.\n- Retrieval/interaction: two-view query (title/abstract + dimension rubric terms), role gating, lexical-overlap reweighting, kind-aware selection (<=6 cards, <=1 episode) and a prepended per-dimension rubric; four instructions now fix the card/episode contract, rubric querying, pattern-only use, and always-on grounding with dimension/subcategory tagging.",
